---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Person structured data — /about is the canonical identity page for the site.
const person = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Trent Jones',
  url: 'https://rtrentjones.dev/about/',
  jobTitle: 'Senior Software Development Engineer',
  worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Audible' },
  alumniOf: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'University of Southern California' },
  knowsAbout: [
    'Software engineering',
    'Developer tooling',
    'Clinical genomics software',
    'Model Context Protocol',
  ],
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/RTrentJones', 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/rtrentjones'],
};
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Trent Jones is a software engineer at Audible, previously on Alexa at Amazon, who started out building software for a clinical genetics lab."
  prose
  structuredData={person}
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Trent, a software engineer. I work at Audible, on the Creator side of the business, and
    before that I spent most of my time at Amazon working on Alexa.
  </p>

  <h2>Experience</h2>

  <dl class="roles">
    <dt>Audible</dt>
    <dd>Software engineering on the Creator side of the business.</dd>

    <dt>Amazon, Alexa</dt>
    <dd>
      Most of my time at Amazon, across web, mobile, backend services, developer tooling, and the
      machinery required to actually ship all of it.
    </dd>

    <dt><a href="https://www.fulgentgenetics.com/">Fulgent Genetics</a></dt>
    <dd>
      Where I started, when the company was still small enough that being a software engineer meant
      working on whatever the lab needed: the LIMS, tools for variant curation and clinical
      reporting, and the patient-facing portal.
    </dd>

    <dt>University of Southern California</dt>
    <dd>Neuroscience and computer science.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p>
    The biology never entirely went away. <a href="/bamcp/">BAMCP</a>, an MCP server for inspecting
    sequencing reads, is the most obvious place it shows up again. The release work did too:
    <a href="/greenlight/">Greenlight</a> came from rebuilding the same deployment and verification
    setup for several different side projects.
  </p>

  <h2>Outside work</h2>

  <p>
    I tend to build things because I want them to exist, or because implementing something seems
    like the best way to understand it. <a href="/pg_kafka/">pg_kafka</a> started with me taking an
    argument about Postgres a little too seriously. <a href="/heistmind/">HeistMind</a> was a tool I
    wanted for a tabletop game. The rest are on the <a href="/projects/">projects page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is where I keep those things and write about what I learned building them, including
    the parts that didn't work the first time.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also find me on <a href="https://github.com/RTrentJones">GitHub</a> and
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rtrentjones">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .roles {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .roles dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .roles dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
</style>
